A||N||6||FieroJoe||Can I make my own tach filter?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||04-25-2001||10:24 PM||||Well, I've got all the symptoms of a dying tach filter.  I know that rodney's got one, but it seems to me like I should be able to make my own.  I know how to make highpass and lowpass filters, with a capacitor and resistor arranged a certain way.  I looked at the pic of rodney's, and it seems that inside that shrink wrap there very well could be just a cap and resistor in there.<P>So, for those of you who understand how it works, is it in fact just a simple filter??  And, if so, do I make a high pass or low pass filter to replace it?<P>In the meantime, I will just bypass it so I can have a tach again.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||04-25-2001||10:38 PM||||Joe,<P>Seems like I remember seeing a "T" filter with a cap and two resistors. The resistors form a voltage divider, and are in series with the tach lead. One side of the cap is connected to the junction of the resistors. The other side of the cap is grounded. I don't remember the values, though. I'll have to poke around. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||04-25-2001||11:19 PM||||Do a search for the word "decipher" somewhere (I think in technical).. I posted it there awhile ago.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||04-26-2001||07:52 AM||||Thanks JohnnyK, thats exactly what I was looking for.  I will have to get to making that as soon as I fix all the ecm codes Im getting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006654.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006654.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-26-2001||09:18 AM||||you don't need a tach filter.. i've taken the one of my 87GT, GTbastards 86SE, BlackGTs 86GT and they are all just fine.. the SE has been off for nearly 3 years and still no problems... my GT has been with out one since july of last year and she's fine too. don't spen $ unless you have too.. granted caps are cheap but still||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||04-26-2001||12:09 PM|||| <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||04-26-2001||05:56 PM||||I love it when my Helms manual says things are there that arent.  I just read in a old tach filter topic that the DIS 4cyl engines dont have a tach filter.<P>edit:  Turned out to be a bad connection in the IP cluster where the pegs on the back of the tach snap in.  Works for now, hopefully they dont loosen up again (I dont want to keep taking that whole thing apart!)<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
